Projects/UOContent/Regions/GuardedRegion.cs

Adds a shard rule: a wild creature that attacks on sight (fight mode Closest, Strongest or Weakest; not tamed, not
summoned by a player, not invulnerable) whose combatant is a player or a player's pet is a guard candidate inside a
guarded region, whoever struck first. New public helpers: IsMenace, IsShielded, IsHostileCreature, IsPlayerSide and
IsCallable. Two settings: guards.hostileCreatures (on by default) and guards.hostileCreaturesForClients (off by
default, so a player at the keyboard keeps the stock rule; only players with no client, the shard's bots, are
covered). Without this patch BotAIv2 does not compile.

WHY. Patrick, 02.10.2026: a bot beaten on the road that cannot win must run to town, because the guards are supposed
to kill hostile creatures that fight within the town limits. They did not. A bot that swung once at the creature is
never innocent to it again while the chase goes on: every bite refreshes the bot's own entry in the creature's
aggressors (Mobile.AggressiveAction), so the creature never turns criminal towards it. A creature made criminal on
the road is not on the town's list either, and most deaths in town came after the run had ended, when nobody called.
Build 429 counted 0 guard kills of 78 pursuers.

